e prefect orion so  orion is what prefect right now is in  version 0.15  orion will basically be our 2.0 and  orion has a lot of like  breaking changes based on of of the you  know previous three years that uh where  prefect you know supported people in  their workflows and realized that there  were a lot of fundamental things that if  we could uh you know work around then we  could provide a much smoother developer  experience for  uh building workflows and so i'll also  uh show orion later on right now orion  is in technical preview so you can go uh  spin it up try it out yourself uh it's  open source as well  uh and it is  pretty different from any other  orchestration framework out there and  i'll explain that later  so first we're going to see the current  prefect core  so now we have this this uh orion and we  have current prefix core pre the one uh  for production workflows today you would  still use prefix core as a rhinostone  technical preview and prefect core i  mentioned this in version 0.15 we're  steadily going to make that a 1.0 pretty  soon after we stabilize it  just a bit but i mean it is very stable  it is used by a lot of companies in  production workflows already  so for  our motivation today what we want to do  is we want to track dogecoin prices and  we just want to be alerted when there's  a dip in dogecoin price  and when i was preparing when i first  prepared this talk uh in the death uh  for the death summit earlier in may  there was this major uh dip in crypto  everything just down ten percent  uh it was it's quite shocking i mean i  don't trade crypto myself i don't know  if we have anyone out there who does  but yeah in general we want we're  interested in capturing these like dips  so that we could get an alert  so first we're gonna do this in  pure native python without prefect right  and we have two functions so there's  going to be four steps number one we're  gonna make a url  number two just a simple request for  that uh to get the data number three the  actual check for dips and then lastly  we're going to send ourselves a slack  notification only if there is a dip  so here we have the first function  the only thing you really need to know  is we're hitting the coindesk api  and we are passing in a coin  and this coin will be plugged into the  url  so that and we'll just return this url  and then this get data function we're  just gonna do a get request to that api  and then we'll we're gonna get the  um a data frame  of the results and pass out that data  frame  and then we have our detect  dip function so we just get our data  frame  get the peak get the bottom um  there there will be uh  the data changes every minute  so we will just be getting 10 minutes of  data so just like a 10 minute window 10  measurements  and  we'll just check the max of that the min  of that see if there was like a major  percent you know dip  if there was will return true uh if  there wasn't low return false uh there's  a threshold here so this is like 10  dip that we're expecting  and if you're to put this in production  what you would do is something like you  know create maybe create an ec2 instance  uh make an infinite loop to be run every  five minutes  we're gonna  get our data uh  check if there's a dip and then there's  a dip we'll post to slack so i didn't  implement the post to slack yet because  it's going to be a lot easier in prefect  and i'll show  how later  but uh in general we have this up and  running and again with negative  engineering there's many things that can  go wrong right so like what happens if  the api fails the hitting the coindesk  api  well maybe we could code retries  ourselves right or what happens if we  wanted to track another coin instead of  dogecoin well i had i'd have to spin up  another process change the dodge there  and then  run that separate process  what happens if we wanted off schedule  runs uh besides this three like we  wanted a run now right instead of this  3